INSERT INTO `ha_term_relationships` (`object_id`,`term_taxonomy_id`,`term_order`) SELECT @translation_id,tt.term_taxonomy_id,0 FROM `ha_term_taxonomy` tt JOIN `ha_terms` t ON t.term_id=tt.term_id WHERE @translation_id IS NOT NULL AND tt.taxonomy='category' AND t.slug='iraq' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `ha_term_relationships` r WHERE r.object_id=@translation_id AND r.term_taxonomy_id=tt.term_taxonomy_id) LIMIT 1;
INSERT INTO `ha_posts` (`post_author`,`post_date`,`post_date_gmt`,`post_content`,`post_title`,`post_excerpt`,`post_status`,`comment_status`,`ping_status`,`post_name`,`post_modified`,`post_modified_gmt`,`post_parent`,`guid`,`menu_order`,`post_type`,`post_mime_type`,`comment_count`) SELECT 1,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),'<p>Determining <strong>Mung Bean Seed Rate per Hectare</strong> It is one of the most important management decisions for farmers, directly affecting final crop yield, total costs, and seedling survival until final root establishment. Considering that plant and seedling density per hectare must be calculated precisely based on climatic conditions and seed movement and irrigation methods suitable for drip and tape irrigation, this article provides a comprehensive guide to recommended seeding rates, factors affecting appropriate density, and best seed movement methods using drip and tape irrigation.</p>\n<p>Mung bean, due to its seed structure and unsuitability for continuous direct and broadcast sowing, is one of the crop plants where the mung bean seed rate per hectare directly affects final crop yield and total costs. The objective of this section is to examine practical methods for determining the mung bean seed rate per hectare under different sowing and irrigation conditions.</p>\n<h2>Introduction to Mung Bean and the Importance of Seed Count in Determining Appropriate Density</h2>\n<p>Mung bean is a leguminous crop with a short to medium growth cycle, having the highest popularity in the warm and low-rainfall regions of Iran. Mung bean seed count can affect seed consumption, seed purchase costs, and ultimately final crop yield and subsequent sowing continuity. Accurate determination of mung bean seed rate per hectare requires examining several factors such as climate type, soil type, irrigation method, and sowing time.</p>\n<p></p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مقدار-بذر-ماش-در-هکتار-راهنمای-جامع-تصویر-شاخص.webp" alt="مقدار بذر ماش در هکتار: راهنمای جامع - تصویر 1"/><figcaption>seed rate per hectare crop mung bean</figcaption></figure>\n<h3>Factors Affecting Mung Bean Seed Rate per Hectare</h3>\n<p>The accuracy in determining the precise seed quantity required for one hectare of mung bean depends on several factors. These factors can affect the final crop yield and the survival of seedlings and plant root systems. The seed count of mung bean is directly related to the plant population per hectare and the space for root growth. Under drip and strip irrigation conditions, an appropriate planting density must be used so that plants can grow well and access their root zones. Additionally, the type of irrigation and sowing time can influence the mung bean seed rate per hectare. Given the importance of this issue, a thorough examination of these factors is necessary to achieve the best results in final crop yield and the sustainability of subsequent plantings.</p>\n<h2>Mung bean seed rate per hectare based on sowing methods</h2>\n<p>The mung bean sowing method is one of the most important factors determining the required seed quantity. Common mung bean sowing methods include broadcast, row, and mixed sowing. Each of these methods affects the mung bean seed count per hectare. In broadcast sowing, seeds are distributed uniformly across one hectare, and the seed count directly impacts the number of plants per hectare and the space for root growth. In row sowing, seeds are planted in designated rows, and the seed count directly impacts the number of plants per hectare and the space for root growth. In mixed sowing, a combination of broadcast and row methods is used, and the seed count directly impacts the number of plants per hectare and the space for root growth. Under drip and strip irrigation conditions, row sowing is recommended to ensure mung bean seeds are planted uniformly per hectare, allowing plants to grow well and access their root zones.</p>\n<p></p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مقدار-بذر-ماش-در-هکتار-راهنمای-جامع-کاربرد-عملی.webp" alt="مقدار بذر ماش در هکتار: راهنمای جامع - تصویر 2"/><figcaption>seed rate per hectare crop mung bean</figcaption></figure>\n<h2>The Impact of Drip and Tape Irrigation on Mung Bean Seed Density</h2>\n<p>Drip and tape irrigation are two common methods of irrigating mung beans in Iran, which influence the amount of mung bean seed per hectare. In drip irrigation, water reaches the plant roots directly and uniformly, and the mung bean seed count directly affects the number of plants per hectare and the root growth space. In tape irrigation, water reaches the plant roots in a strip-like and uniform manner, and the mung bean seed count directly affects the number of plants per hectare and the root growth space. Under drip and tape irrigation conditions, an appropriate density must be used to ensure plants can grow well and access root zones. Additionally, the type of irrigation and planting time can affect the amount of mung bean seed per hectare. Given the importance of these factors, a thorough examination is necessary to achieve the best results in final yield efficiency and the sustainability of subsequent crops. For more information on how to determine tape irrigation points, please <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d9%86%d8%ad%d9%88%d9%87-%d8%aa%d8%b9%db%8c%db%8c%d9%86-%d9%86%d9%82%d8%a7%d8%b7-%d8%a2%d8%a8%db%8c%d8%a7%d8%b1%db%8c-%d9%86%d9%88%d8%a7%d8%b1-%d8%aa%db%8c%d9%be/">How to Determine Tape Irrigation Points</a> refer to the following.</p>\n<h2>Practical Guide to Mung Bean Seed Placement and Optimal Density Calculation</h2>\n<p>Fava bean seed placement directly affects final yield efficiency and the survival of plant roots. To establish fava bean seeds, appropriate plant density must be used to ensure good growth and root access. Under drip irrigation and tape line systems, suitable planting density is required to allow plants to grow well and develop root systems. Additionally, irrigation type and planting time can influence the amount of fava bean seed per hectare. Given the importance of these factors, careful analysis is essential to achieve optimal final yield efficiency and continuity in subsequent cropping seasons.</p>\n<p>As a practical example, in one hectare of fava bean crops using drip irrigation, seed rate can influence the number of plants per hectare and the space available for root growth. Considering the significance of this matter, a detailed review of these factors is necessary to achieve the best results in final yield efficiency and the sustainability of future plantings.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مقدار-بذر-ماش-در-هکتار-راهنمای-جامع-جزئیات-فنی.webp" alt="مقدار بذر ماش در هکتار: راهنمای جامع - تصویر 3"/><figcaption>Fava bean seed rate per hectare</figcaption></figure>\n<p></p>\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions About Fava Bean Seed Rate Per Hectare</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>What is the fava bean seed rate per hectare under drip irrigation and tape line conditions?</strong><br>Under drip irrigation and tape line conditions, the fava bean seed rate per hectare directly affects the number of plants per hectare and the growth space for roots. Given the importance of this issue, a thorough examination of these factors is essential to achieve optimal results in final yield efficiency and the continuity of subsequent crops.</li>\n<li><strong>Do broadcast and row planting methods significantly affect the fava bean seed rate per hectare?</strong><br>The broadcasting and row planting methods directly affect the mung bean seed rate per hectare, the plant density per hectare, and the root growth space. Considering the importance of this, a detailed examination of these factors is essential to achieve the best results in final crop yield and the sustainability of subsequent crops.</li>\n<li><strong>Does the planting time have a significant effect on the mung bean seed rate per hectare?</strong><br>The planting time directly affects the mung bean seed rate per hectare, the plant density per hectare, and the root growth space. Considering the importance of this, a detailed examination of these factors is essential to achieve the best results in final crop yield and the sustainability of subsequent crops.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Conclusion and final recommendations for farmers</h2>\n<p>This article provides a comprehensive guide on recommended plant population, factors affecting optimal density, and best practices for seed placement using drip and tape irrigation for crops like mung beans. Determining the exact mung bean seed rate per hectare requires examining several factors such as climate type, soil type, irrigation method, and planting time. Under drip and tape irrigation conditions, it is best to use row planting to ensure mung bean seeds are sown uniformly per hectare, allowing plants to grow well and access nutrients. Additionally, the type of irrigation and planting time can affect the mung bean seed rate per hectare. Given the importance of this, a precise analysis of these factors is necessary to achieve the best results in final crop yield and continuity of subsequent crops. For more information on Hamdani alfalfa seed rate per hectare + influencing factors and black-eyed pea seed rate per hectare + influencing factors, you can refer to our articles. Also, the 3-inch play pipe is one of the most important pieces of equipment for drip and tape irrigation that must be considered when planting mung beans.</p>\n<p><strong>Related articles:</strong> <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/potato-drip-tape-complete-guide/">potato drip tape complete guide</a>، <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/ch-enkuniyi-fiori-ob-baroi-banda-tomizi/">ch enkuniyi fiori ob baroi banda tomizi</a>، <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/lettuce-seed-quantity-per-hectare-irrigation-tips/">lettuce seed quantity per hectare irrigation tips</a></p>','Fava Bean Seed Rate per Hectare: A Comprehensive Guide for Drip and Tape Row Irrigation','The chickpea seed rate per hectare directly affects final harvest yield. This article provides a comprehensive guide to recommended seed counts, factors influencing optimal density, and best practices for sowing with drip irrigation and strip mulching. Read on to learn how to avoid common errors in determining seed density and achieve the best performance.','publish','closed','closed','fava-bean-seed-rate-per-hectare-drip-tape-irrigation-guide',NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),0,'',0,'post','',0 WHERE @source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @translation_id IS NULL AND @slug_conflict IS NULL;
INSERT INTO `ha_postmeta` (`post_id`,`meta_key`,`meta_value`) SELECT @translation_id,'_navar_translation_queue_key','article-translation:crop-311:en-US' WHERE @translation_id IS NOT NULL AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `ha_postmeta` WHERE post_id=@translation_id AND meta_key='_navar_translation_queue_key');
